 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the city of New York to reduce the interest accrued on\ncertain charges assessed on real property located at 1690 60th Street in\nBrooklyn",
    "basePrintNo": "S6225",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6225-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6225\n\nSPONSOR: FELDER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the city of New York to reduce the interest accrued\non certain charges assessed on real property located at 1690 60th Street\nin Brooklyn\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo rectify a bureaucratic process in which, at this time, the City of\nNew York is unable to amend accrued interest charges despite the organ-\nization's intent to pay.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill indicates that the City of New York shall reduce\nthe interest accrued on charges assessed by the New York City Department\nof Health for inspections, clean-ups, examinations and other services\nperformed between January 21, 1997 and November 9, 1999 on the property\nlocated at 1690 60th street in Brooklyn, New York.\n\nSection 2 of the bill sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPrior to the purchasing of the property located at 1690 60th Street\nBrooklyn, the New York City Department of Health accessed a pest-control\nand clean-up charge of approximately $34,000.00. These charges were\nchallenged but not removed, and at closing, the charges were marked\n\"omit.\" Over the years, these charges remained and grew to over\n$1,375,000.00.\n\nWhile the funds to pay the original penalty were held in escrow, the\ninterest continued to accrue. This bill is intended to rectify the\nunjustly accumulated interest charges and restore the amount to the\noriginal fine.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act would take effect immediately.\n",
